    "body": "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Closed without merge and superseded by the mechanism-first #969 pivot.** This patch is an immutable review record of the disclosed capacity census; it does not close #969, deliver a terminal programme result, or leave #974 active. #969 absorbed the repair and decoded qualification scope.\n\n## Outcome\n\nReferences #969.\n\nHistorical census status: `REDESIGN_NON_H4_ORDERED_TRANSPORT_REPRESENTATION`.\n\nThis closed patch recorded the #969 Phase 0A individual-channel capacity census and the then-proposed #974 successor before the pivot. It does not implement #953, A1Q-H, correctness, reasoning, chat, optimization, formal closure, release QA, or broad generation.\n\n## Roadmap and native graph correction\n\n- #969 is A1Q-L: non-H4 capacity preflight, conditional one selector, Gate 0, and current/previous/last-two/sentence only.\n- #973 is A1Q-H: paragraph/conversation/global only after accepted local/sentence attention and #953 decoded generation.\n- #954 remains natively blocked by #953 and #973; the #954 -> #955 -> #962 -> #963 -> #964 -> #965 chain is unchanged.\n- Living AGENTS/ROADMAP/programme/evaluation/RESEARCH prose now reflects PR #972/#970 closure and the corrected scope.\n- The observed negative created unassigned child #974. #974 is blocked by #969 and blocks both #953 and #973. The disclosed #969 population is regression-only for #974; #974 must freeze a new independent split.\n\n## Frozen construction and validation\n\nPublic pre-evidence ledger: https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/issues/969#issuecomment-5442538688\n\n- construction `A1QL-CAPACITY-CONSTRUCTION-1`: `blake3:acf865c43e6d6ce3ba2a39e553047c2e19d535673e4a96b915f463423fda53d4`\n- sealed validation `A1QL-CAPACITY-VALIDATION-1`: `blake3:17a2e2716b236912df83c52bfa5eb2f09652740232b821e982cffeca39e3d9ec`\n- public contract: `blake3:f63dd5939745286b1c88e7a1da2dedad81493b038f0ef5dead4ecac29d479f55`\n- canonical report: `blake3:da72cd766bdc2a938286a44de0be60a66242ed9691a02add025e1ea3609b7ae5`\n\nThe six same-length/same-multiset histories share suffix `[aa,qq]`, natural union `{ll,rr}`, and equal support/work. S4 parity determines behavior: EVEN selects `ll`; ODD selects `rr`. Both target-free split structures are prepared before the separate label ledgers are joined.\n\nPer split: 3 histories, 6 candidate decisions, 21 row reads, 6 exact payload inversions. Per query: 7 rows, candidate-entry ceiling 56, candidate ceiling 8, maximum admitted 2, direct exact-row miss, no target injection, and no future visibility.\n\n## Channel-capacity result\n\n| Channel | Order | Candidate | Same candidate | Classes/purity | Coverage | Oracle | Transfer decisions | Transfer queries |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| each of six available history-only channels | 0/15 | 0/6 | 0/30 | 1 impure | 6/6 | 3/6 | 0/6 | 0/3 |\n| session + candidate S3 direct pair | 0/15 | 6/6 | 0/30 | 2 impure | 6/6 | 4/6 | 0/6 | 0/3 |\n| real non-digest transported path | 0/0 | 0/0 | 0/0 | unavailable | 0/0 | 0/0 | 0/0 | 0/0 |\n| zeta/n-let/phi typed transition | 0/0 | 0/0 | 0/0 | not exercised: no public typed rule | 0/0 | 0/0 | 0/0 | 0/0 |\n\nThe candidate pair is explicitly `PAIR_NO_INTERACTION`: appending static candidate state does not recover aliased history. Every eligible non-H4, non-digest channel key has 0/15 earlier-order sensitivity on this frozen split, and no real non-digest transported-path field is exposed. The separate ordered-H4 commitment and #967 state remain structural evidence and are not invalidated.\n\n## Hard stop and controls\n\nNo omnibus combination, scalar, selector, validation selection, Gate 0, or sentence fixture was opened. Candidate relabeling, prime-assignment permutation, geometry permutation, current-only, additive, factor, hierarchy-disabled, exact-recall, and path ablations are all reported `NOT_RUN_CHANNEL_CAPACITY_HARD_STOP`, not PASS, because no base channel reached the capacity boundary. Paragraph/conversation/global and downstream product stages are `NOT_RUN` as out of scope.\n\nPreserved: reversible codec, schema-2 natural support/admission, exact payload inversion, paired-H4/heatmap structural state, and incremental hierarchy plumbing.\n\n## Focused checks\n\n- #969 identity + double-execution capacity probe: PASS, 2/2 tests\n- #952 regression: PASS\n- #967 regression: PASS\n- #970 regression: PASS\n- focused `uor-r4-core` all-target compilation: PASS (pre-existing unrelated warnings only)\n- exact local source-closure check: PASS\n- WASM library check: PASS (pre-existing unrelated warnings only)\n- format check: PASS\n- diff check: PASS\n- claim-wording check: PASS\n\nNOT RUN locally: workspace-wide tests/clippy/nextest, teacher/model runs, corpus compiles, generation canaries, fuzz, audit, product QA, correctness, reasoning, chat, performance, formal closure, and release QA. The protected queue remains the repository integration transport; its compatibility jobs are not cited as scientific evidence.\n\n## Nonclaims\n\nThis PR does not establish a selector, local/sentence attention, Gate 0 decoded composition, coherent generation, knowledge, paragraph/conversation/global attention, correctness, reasoning, performance advantage, chat quality, or release readiness. It does not invalidate H4, the exact signed heatmap, zeta phases, n-lets, golden transport, typed geometry, the codec, candidate/value plumbing, or incremental state.",
